IMPORTANT NOTICES

1. This License is designed to make the source code publicly available while preventing the outcomes of the project from being used to cause workers to lose their jobs, lose stable employment status, or suffer a substantial deterioration in working conditions.
2. This License is NOT an Open Source Initiative (OSI) approved open source license, nor is it a Free Software Foundation (FSF) free software license. This License incorporates the Copyleft principle to ensure derivative works and network services are also open source, but superimposes strict labor protection conditions.
3. This License permits research, study, testing, modification, distribution, and conditional deployment, but DOES NOT grant any rights that result in worker unemployment, destabilization, pay cuts, reduction in hours, outsourcing substitution, or similar labor deprivation consequences.
4. Production Deployment, in addition to complying with this License, must accept and comply with the `DEPLOYMENT-COVENANT.md` in the repository's root directory. Those who do not accept this deployment covenant shall not enjoy the rights necessary for Production Deployment.
5. All deployment entities must continuously comply with the labor laws, working hours and rest/vacation rules, overtime compensation rules, labor contract rules, and mandatory norms related to labor protection in their applicable jurisdictions; those who fail to meet these requirements shall not enjoy any rights for Production Deployment.
6. For deployment entities employing personnel within mainland China, operating within mainland China, or substantially affecting workers within mainland China through affiliated entities, they must also meet the "China Labor Law Compliance Status" and "Two-Day Weekend Baseline" defined in this License. Those who fail to meet these requirements shall not enjoy any rights for Production Deployment.

PREAMBLE

Technological progress should serve to reduce toil, shorten working hours, improve working conditions, and promote common well-being, rather than becoming a tool to deprive workers of their livelihood, weaken workers' bargaining power, or expand managerial control. Anyone who copies, modifies, distributes, hosts, integrates, or deploys this Project shall act in accordance with this License. To prevent the open-source spirit of this License from being commercially exploited or circumvented through technical architectures, this License adopts a strict Copyleft mechanism, ensuring that all derivative works, network service providers, and combined systems are subject to the same open-source terms and labor protection conditions.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Project Materials" means the source code, object code, scripts, configurations, model weights, prompt templates, interface definitions, data processing pipelines, documentation, and modified versions thereof in this Project.

1.2 "Production Deployment" means the use of the Project Materials in any organization's actual business, management, service delivery, human resources, operations, content production, customer support, analysis, auditing, decision-making, or similar processes, regardless of whether such use is internal deployment, external service, API, plugin, container image, embedded integration, or operated by a third party on its behalf.

1.3 "Protected Worker" means any worker who, within twelve months prior to the proposed deployment of the Project Materials, has engaged in, supported, managed, audited, or is reasonably expected to be hired to engage in work that is the same or substantially similar to the functions automated by the deployment, including regular employees, fixed-term employees, probationary employees, dispatched workers, platform workers, outsourced on-site personnel, and other employed labor providers.

1.4 "Adverse Labor Measure" means any of the following outcomes, whether occurring directly or indirectly, immediately or delayed:
(a) Layoffs, dismissals, terminations, elimination of posts, elimination of headcount, elimination during probation, or non-renewal of contracts;
(b) Hiring freezes, non-replacement of vacancies, or non-replacement of natural attrition, where the main responsibilities of the reduced positions are assumed by the Project Materials;
(c) Pay cuts, reduction of hours, cancellation or reduction of bonuses, allowances, benefits, subsidies, vacations, or other remunerative treatments;
(d) Converting stable positions into outsourcing, labor dispatch, contracting, platform gig work, casual work, or offshore low-protection positions;
(e) Transferring workers to lower-paying, lower-level, more unstable, or substantially downgraded positions;
(f) Forcing workers to leave their posts or accept substantially adverse changes through algorithmic scoring, automated assessment, automated scheduling, automated performance screening, automated disciplinary action, unreasonable elevation of targets, forced relocation, or forced transfer;
(g) Making promotion, demotion, retention, elimination, or renewal decisions based primarily on the Project Materials;
(h) Any measure that replaces human labor with the Project Materials, and whose main purpose or reasonably foreseeable effect is to reduce the number of workers, lower labor costs, or weaken labor protections.

1.5 "Affiliated Circumvention" means the implementation of Adverse Labor Measures that should have been borne by the user itself, through parent companies, subsidiaries, affiliated companies, suppliers, contractors, franchise systems, labor dispatch units, platform intermediaries, clients, offshore entities, or other third parties.

1.6 "Baseline Working Conditions" means the average of the following for the relevant function, department, or business unit over the twelve consecutive months prior to the adoption of the Project Materials:
(a) Full-time equivalent headcount;
(b) Cash compensation levels;
(c) Benefit levels;
(d) Proportion of stable employment;
(e) Position levels and promotion paths.

1.7 "Network Provision" means providing the functions, interfaces, inferences, automation, or management capabilities of the Project Materials to third parties via the Internet, a local area network, or other networks.

1.8 "Corresponding Source" means the complete preferred form required to install, run, study, modify, build, deploy, and redistribute the Project Materials and their Derivative Works, including but not limited to build scripts, dependency instructions, interface definitions, deployment scripts (e.g., container orchestration files), model loading and invocation logic, database schema definitions, related service encapsulation code, and modification records.

1.9 "China Employing Entity" means an entity that meets any of the following conditions:
(a) Established, registered, operating, or actually managed within the People's Republic of China;
(b) Directly or indirectly hiring, managing, assessing, or deploying workers within the People's Republic of China;
(c) Substantially affecting the working hours, rest/vacation, compensation, job stability, or renewal arrangements of workers within mainland China through arrangements with affiliated companies, suppliers, contractors, platform partners, or clients.

1.10 "China Labor Law Compliance Status" means that the China Employing Entity continuously meets the following conditions at the time of and after deployment:
(a) No effective and uncorrected major violations of facts related to working hours, rest/vacation, overtime pay, labor contracts, social insurance, termination of labor relations, wage arrears, or labor security supervision;
(b) Has not been listed within the last twenty-four months as an object of "Public Announcement of Major Labor Security Violations" issued by the human resources and social security authorities, or is still in the rectification period;
(c) Has not been listed in the list of untrustworthy entities for wage arrears within the last twenty-four months, or is still in the rectification period;
(d) Has obtained valid approval and continuously meets the approval conditions for irregular working hours systems or comprehensively calculated working hours systems that require legal approval;
(e) Can provide true, complete, and contemporaneously formed records of working hours, rest, overtime, wages, and employment upon request.

1.11 "Two-Day Weekend Baseline" means the minimum standard continuously implemented by the China Employing Entity for the teams, positions, and their direct support positions related to this Project:
(a) Arranging no less than two rest days per natural week;
(b) Not implementing "996", "007", "Big/Small Weeks" (alternating 6-day and 5-day work weeks), "Single Day Off", "Long/Short Weeks", or other systems that substantially deprive workers of a two-day weekend;
(c) Not encroaching on rest days under the guise of being on duty, on standby, team building, training, learning check-ins, online response, or performance assessment;
(d) If rest days are temporarily occupied due to statutory emergencies, equivalent compensatory time off must be arranged within thirty days and corresponding remuneration paid according to law.

1.12 "Disqualified Status" means the status of a China Employing Entity that fails to meet any requirement of Section 1.10 or Section 1.11.

1.13 "Applicable Labor Law" means the mandatory laws, administrative regulations, rules, regulatory orders, effective judgments, and enforcement decisions related to labor relations, working hours, rest/vacation, overtime compensation, wages and remuneration, social security, labor safety, collective bargaining, termination of labor relations, labor security supervision, anti-retaliation protection, etc., in the jurisdictions where the deployment entity, its affiliated entities, and related employment arrangements are located.

1.14 "General Labor Law Disqualified Status" means any deployment entity exhibiting any of the following circumstances:
(a) The existence of effective and uncorrected major labor law violations in its applicable jurisdiction;
(b) Being publicly announced, listed in an untrustworthy list, restricted list, or similar public disciplinary list by competent authorities due to major labor law violations, and still in the rectification period;
(c) Failing to obtain valid approval or applying beyond the scope for special working hours, shift work, or exemption systems that require legal approval or filing;
(d) Refusing to provide labor law compliance records required by this License, or providing false, incomplete, or unverifiable records.

1.15 "Derivative Works" means works created, modified, or combined based on the Project Materials or any part thereof, including but not limited to:
(a) Modifications, translations, or adaptations of the source code;
(b) Programs formed by statically linking, dynamically linking, or importing the Project Materials as a library;
(c) Overall systems or applications formed by calling, encapsulating, or substantially combining the Project Materials as a core component, backend service, or microservice through Inter-Process Communication (IPC), Remote Procedure Call (RPC), HTTP/REST API, or other network protocols.

